      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Facial pain is a common presenting symptom in oral surgery outpatient clinics. Among the large number of patients presenting in this way, a small number of patients will be found to have intracranial tumours. Three such cases are described and recommendations made regarding the selection of facial pain patients for further investigation."},
